eature_054 now.\n\nFor feature_012=1 versus 0, H33 is null and its interval excludes the positive clinical threshold, so it is rejected. H31 and H32 have small positive signed estimates (about 0.005-0.007), far below threshold, although their intervals just include the positive threshold. These are unresolved but not active follow-up targets because they are not clinically supported and do not replicate the predictor pattern across outcomes.\n\nFor feature_050=1 versus 0, H34 is null within clinical bounds and is rejected. H35 and H36 have tiny positive signed estimates (about 0.005 and 0.003), with intervals that extend beyond threshold but are dominated by uncertainty. These are unresolved and deferred; the predictor does not show a credible, direction-consistent clinically meaningful signal.\n\nOverall, the new 12-test screen produced no accepted claims and no predictor-outcome pair with a clinically meaningful point estimate plus interval support. The several intervals that remain compatible with threshold effects are too imprecise and too exploratory for validation, especially given prior multiplicity and the earlier failure of feature_042 on independent validation. I request no validation at this stage. H2 and H10 remain active because they are the best existing but still weak candidates; if later evidence strengthens one, validation could be considered. All statements remain limited to associations within the supplied dataset, not causal effects or generalizable claims."
